@meeting pu3.offer.party
// SW3: the offer at the storm's all-clear party (Day 14, Sunday, bow lounge, 19:00-21:00). Calder walks up to you
// through the party; the lounge turns to look; Halloran and Tomas are there (if one isn't, 24u can drop his lines, as
// the FLC does with a missing cast member). Same two replies in the same order as pu3.offer. Friends' luck (pu3.luck,
// the raised cups) follows it in bubbles.
title: Your next test
from: Chief Ines Calder
gist: At the storm party, Calder told you in front of the lounge: your Tier 3 test is tomorrow, Monday, at 09:00. Pass it and you're a Senior Officer.
== lines
calder > you: Don't put your cup down. This won't take long.   [gesture]
calder: Relied on. And the storm counted. Every repair of it.
calder: Monday. Tomorrow, then. Your Tier 3 test, nine o'clock, on the board.
halloran-emeka: Tier 3? At two weeks aboard? Some of us took a year.   [laugh]
halloran-emeka: I'm not bitter. I'm a little bitter. Well done, you.
? choice
* Tomorrow, then. I'll be ready.   rel:calder+2
  calder: I know. One more cup of tea, then bed. Not two.   [nod]
* At a party? You couldn't wait till morning?   rel:calder+2
  calder: No. I wanted to see your face. There it is. Good.   [nod]
tomas > you: Tomorrow's the big one? Go to bed early. Not yet. After this song.   [laugh]
calder: Pass it and you're a Senior Officer. Enjoy the party. Not too much.
